Convex 1.44.0. A document has this shape:

```ts
{
  metadata: {
    title: string,
    author: { name: string, contact: { email: string, phone?: string } },
    tags: string[]
  },
  content: string
}
```

Inside a mutation, `doc` is the existing document fetched using `args.documentId`; a missing document has already caused an error. `args.author` is validated as a complete replacement author with the shape above.

options.text:
```ts
await ctx.db.patch("documents", args.documentId, {
  metadata: { ...doc.metadata, author: args.author },
});
```

```ts
await ctx.db.patch("documents", args.documentId, {
  metadata: { author: args.author },
});
```

```ts
await ctx.db.patch("documents", args.documentId, {
  metadata: {
    ...doc.metadata,
    author: {
      ...args.author,
      contact: { ...doc.metadata.author.contact, ...args.author.contact },
    },
  },
});
```
